\section dls Modifications at DLS

These are notes on the modifications from the original vendor software.

The software was delivered on a Debian PC running the EPICS distribution as packaged by NSLS-II.

The paths were modified to match DLS specific locations.

The csvlogger sequencer program uses the environment variable "HOME" to determine where files are written to.

The IOC runs as user "cryocooler" on the Debian PC supplied and the
log files were being saved to hard disk at the location
/home/cryocooler/CCXV_DATA. The ioc startup script was modified to set
HOME to save files under the path /dls/ops-data/CryoCooler/${IOCNAME}

Similarly, the alarms are written under "HOME" to the file alarms.log
by the FileLog component. The environment modification of HOME applies
to this file too.

**/

